A DLL mod that lets you customize your character's attack, movement, skill and spell casting speed, and Torrent's too, all in the config file.

[size=4][b]Why this mod?[/b][/size]
[i]Ever wind up a greatsword swing, watch the boss stroll out of range, and still have to finish the whole animation? Or stand there mid-cast while an enemy walks right up and hits you?

So I made this mod: every action your character takes gets a bit snappier - running, rolling, swinging, casting - and Torrent finally gallops like he means it. Keep it subtle, or crank it up and play in fast-forward.[/i]

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Faster walking, sneaking (10% by default) and running (20% by default).[/*]
[*]Faster attacks (20% by default).[/*]
[*]Faster rolling (10% by default).[/*]
[*]Faster skills (20% by default).[/*]
[*]Faster sorceries and incantations (20% by default).[/*]
[*]Faster Torrent: walking 10% and galloping 30% by default.[/*]
[*]Hotkey to reload the config file without restarting the game.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Notes[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Every multiplier goes from 0.1 (slow motion) to 10 - 1 is vanilla.[/*]
[*]The master multiplier speeds up every action, even getting hit.[/*]
[*]Known issue: the item speed only applies when you use an item standing still - drinking a flask while moving follows the movement animations instead.[/*]
[/list]

[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/4333/images/11173/11173-1790700260-1476558279.gif[/img]

[size=4][b][color=#E74C3C]Disclaimer: Only use in offline mode with EAC disabled![/color][/b][/size]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

Any DLL mod loader works, e.g. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/117]Elden Mod Loader[/url], [url=https://github.com/soulsmods/ModEngine2/releases]Mod Engine 2[/url], [url=https://github.com/garyttierney/me3/releases]Mod Engine 3[/url].

[b]Option 1 - [url=https://github.com/soulsmods/ModEngine2/releases]Mod Engine 2[/url] (recommended)[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download Mod Engine 2 from the link above and extract it into your game folder (the same folder as [i]eldenring.exe[/i]).[/*]
[*]Download this mod, then create a folder to hold it and its config file - for example, inside your game folder create a [b]natives[/b] folder.[/*]
[*]Open [b]config_eldenring.toml[/b] and edit [b]external_dlls = [ ][/b] to add the DLL, e.g.:
[code]external_dlls = [
    "natives\\SpeedMultiplier.dll",
][/code]
[/*]
[*]Launch the game using Mod Engine 2's launcher, [b]modengine2_launcher.exe[/b].[/*]
[/list]

[b]Option 2 - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/117]Elden Mod Loader[/url][/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download Elden Mod Loader from the link above and extract it into your game folder.[/*]
[*]Download this mod and drag [b]SpeedMultiplier.dll[/b] and [b]SpeedMultiplier.toml[/b] into the [b]mods[/b] folder.[/*]
[*]Launch the game - the mod will be loaded automatically.[/*]
[/list]

